863: ### 5.2 Active-Low Failsafe Invariant Test
864: A dedicated unit test verifying both polarities of bit 7:
865: ```rust
866: #[test]
867: fn test_osd_active_low_failsafe_invariant() {
868:     let mut payload = vec![0u8; 53];
869:     
870:     // Case 1: Bit 7 == 0 -> Failsafe MUST BE TRUE (Active)
871:     LittleEndian::write_u32(&mut payload[32..36], 0x0000_0000);
872:     let osd1 = OsdRecord::parse(&payload).unwrap();
873:     assert!(osd1.flight_status.is_failsafe_active());
874: 
875:     // Case 2: Bit 7 == 1 -> Failsafe MUST BE FALSE (Inactive)
876:     LittleEndian::write_u32(&mut payload[32..36], 0x0000_0080);
877:     let osd2 = OsdRecord::parse(&payload).unwrap();
878:     assert!(!osd2.flight_status.is_failsafe_active());
879: }
880: ```
